## Library Overview
The python-mysql-replication project is a Pure Python Implementation of MySQL replication protocol build on top of PyMYSQL. It's a binlog-based Change Data Capture (CDC) library available on PyPI.

## Maintenance Status
The project was updated on Oct 25, 2024, indicating recent activity. The project is tested with MySQL 5.5, 5.6, 5.7, 8.0.14, MariaDB 10.6, and Python 3.7, 3.11, with PyPy 3.7 and 3.9 support.

## Production Use
The project is used in production for critical stuff in some medium internet corporations, though not all use cases have been perfectly tested in the real world.

## Use Cases
Use cases include MySQL to NoSQL database replication, MySQL to search engine replication, cache invalidation when database changes, audit, and real time analytics.

