# NATS Toolchain — Phase 1, Step A1

Companion to [Design.md §11](../../Design.md#11-phase-1--detailed-breakdown) (Track A) and [Dependencies.md](../../Dependencies.md), which is the source of truth for these pins going forward.

## Pinned versions

| Tool | Version | Released | How it's used here |
|---|---|---|---|
| `nats-server` | **2.14.5** | 2026-08-12 | Consumed via the official Docker image (`nats:2.14.5`), pinned in `docker-compose.yml` (§11 Track A6) — **not installed locally**. |
| `nsc` | **2.15.0** | 2026-06-02 (year not explicit in source snippet at time of research — verify against the [releases page](https://github.com/nats-io/nsc/releases) if it matters) | Installed locally; drives the bootstrap script (A3) that issues the Operator/Account/User JWTs. |
| `nats` CLI (`natscli`) | **0.4.0** | 2026-05-01 (same caveat as above) | Installed locally; used for the manual smoke test (A7) — pub/sub, stream/KV inspection. |

Re-verify these against the linked release pages before pinning `docker-compose.yml` (A6) or the bootstrap script (A3) — NATS ships frequently.

## Local install (dev machine — Linux)

`nsc` and the `nats` CLI are dev-time tools; install them on your host. `nats-server` itself is **not** installed here — it only runs via the pinned Docker image (A6), so there's nothing to install locally for it.

Both tools are distributed through NATS's official install shim, which fetches the pinned version directly from GitHub releases:

```bash
# nsc — account/JWT management
curl -sf https://binaries.nats.dev/nats-io/nsc/v2@v2.15.0 | sh

# nats CLI — pub/sub, stream/KV inspection, used in the A7 smoke test
curl -sf https://binaries.nats.dev/nats-io/natscli/nats@v0.4.0 | sh
```

Both drop a single binary (`nsc`, `nats`) — the script prompts for (or accepts a flag for) an install directory; make sure it lands somewhere on `$PATH`.

Verify:

```bash
nsc --version
nats --version
```

## Docker image (nats-server)

Referenced here for the record; actually wired into `docker-compose.yml` in step A6:

```
image: nats:2.14.5
```

(An `-alpine` variant exists for a smaller image if that matters later — not required for local dev.)

## Not yet done

This step only pins versions and documents install steps. It does **not** install anything automatically, create the Operator/Account (A3), write `nats-server.conf` (A4), or start any container (A6) — those are separate steps in [Design.md §11](../../Design.md#11-phase-1--detailed-breakdown).
