Based on the search results, here's the information about nsc environment variables and default store locations:

## Default Locations

NSC home lives in ~/.nsc by default and can be changed via the $NSC_HOME environment variable. The nkeys directory by default lives in ~/.nkeys and can be changed via the $NKEYS_PATH environment variable.

## Store Directory

The stores directory lives in $NSC_HOME/nats, which means the default location is `~/.nsc/nats`. This can be changed using the command `nsc env -s <dir>`.

## Summary

| Environment Variable | Default Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `$NSC_HOME` | `~/.nsc` | Stores nsc related data and JWTs |
| `$NKEYS_PATH` | `~/.nkeys` | Stores all private keys |
| Stores Directory | `~/.nsc/nats` | Contains JWTs for operators, accounts, and users |

The contents of the nkeys directory should be treated as secrets.


