What I built:

infra/nats/bootstrap_auth.sh — idempotent, fully containerized (no native installs, consistent with your earlier correction): nsc runs via natsio/nats-box, the manifest is parsed via mikefarah/yq. It creates the Operator, the GSB Account, and one User per entry in adapter_identities.yaml, applies each one's permissions (its manifest subjects + a derived KV-write grant on its own recipient-registration keys + a v1 baseline of $JS.API.>/_INBOX.>/KV-read that every JetStream client needs), generates a .creds file per adapter, and emits the memory-resolver config block for A4.
.gitignore (new) — covers the generated auth material plus the Python/uv patterns Track B will need soon.
Dependencies.md / infra/nats/README.md / Design.md §7.6, §11 — updated with the two new tool pins (yq, and jq noted as an intentional exception to the Docker-only rule since it's a generic host utility, not project-pinned NATS tooling) and a real correction: NATS's idiomatic connection artifact is a single .creds file (JWT+nkey bundled via nsc generate creds), not the separate nkey-seed-path/JWT-path scheme I'd sketched earlier — fixed in §7.6 and the B4 checklist item.
The honest caveat: I don't have Docker available in this environment (checked — docker: command not found), so this script is grounded in nsc's documented CLI reference and nats-box's official README pattern, but has not been run. The existence-check logic (nsc list ... | grep) is the part most likely to need a small fix, since I'm parsing nsc's table output best-effort without having seen it. Please dry-run this against your Docker and tell me what breaks — I'd rather fix it against real output than keep guessing blind.

