nats: error: context deadline exceeded
-- at t=3s, refresh key-a only --
nats: error: context deadline exceeded
-- at t=6s: key-a should be alive (refreshed at t=3), key-b should be expired (never refreshed, ttl=5s) --
nats: error: nats: key not found
---
nats: error: nats: key not found
That failure was a permissions issue in my test, not the mechanism — gsb-admin only has $KV.service-directory.>, and my scratch bucket lived outside that scope. Let me test against the real bucket instead (worth the ~65s wait to validate against actual production config rather than a synthetic one):

Bash Put two test keys into the real service-directory bucket
